### TravelerAPI (Node.js, laboratory works «Розподілені сховища даних») on the SAME database.
### Start: docker compose --profile dds up -d

### 1. Health of the REST API
GET http://localhost:4567/health

### 2. A plan created through the REST API of the labs (it has no owner in Traveler)
POST http://localhost:4567/api/travel-plans
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Чернігів: маршрут вихідного дня (TravelerAPI)",
  "description": "План створено через REST API лабораторних робіт з РСД.",
  "start_date": "2027-09-11",
  "end_date": "2027-09-12",
  "budget": 4000,
  "currency": "UAH",
  "is_public": true
}

> {% client.global.set("planId", response.body.id); %}

### 3. Locations: visit_order is assigned by the API in the same way as in Traveler
POST http://localhost:4567/api/travel-plans/{{planId}}/locations
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Чернігівський Вал", "latitude": 51.4870, "longitude": 31.3055, "budget": 0 }

###
POST http://localhost:4567/api/travel-plans/{{planId}}/locations
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Антонієві печери", "latitude": 51.4815, "longitude": 31.2737, "budget": 120 }

### 4. The plan with its route as the REST API returns it
GET http://localhost:4567/api/travel-plans/{{planId}}
